{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/516293-what-mechanics-do-you-want-in-future-books","id":516293,"title":"What mechanics do you want in future books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-16T10:39:06-07:00","id":516293,"title":"What mechanics do you want in future books?","content":"It's no secret that we all love lore here, but a game is nothing without the rules they run off of. What would you like to see in potential future books?<br /> <br /> For me, I'm hungry for an overhaul of the Cult system. Give me fully fleshed-out rules for having your Cult run off on missions, clashing with other Cults, and all other sorts of goodies; I'd love to see stuff like guidelines for creating high priests and supernatural cultists.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, a thorough exploration of what a Mummy game looks like when you aren't one of the Arisen would be a whole lot of fun. What is it like to be a sadikh, or a cultist, or a Lucid Dead servant? What is it like to pull of heists in the name of relic-theivery? How is it to face off against federal agencies and rival groups?<br /> <br /> Other than that, more Relics are always wanted, as are more antagonists - like those dedicated to stopping the Arisen from acting in Asia (mentioned in Guildhalls), or new pieces for Amkhata building - and the oft-mentioned mortal sorcerers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thanke