rum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/516293-what-mechanics-do-you-want-in-future-books?p=516312#post516312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooooooooo more stuff like Assassin's Creed Brotherhood?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, a sadikh already has his past lives inside his head, and the Pieces of Eden do make good Relics...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T16:24:56-07:00","id":516533,"title":"","content":"Relic architecture. D.C. promised <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T05:18:30-07:00","id":516943,"title":"","content":"<b>Night Horrors: Eternity Awaits</b><ul><li><b>Chapter 1: Unending Servitude</b> details significant mortals, cultists, sadikh, and Witnesses. Also mortal sorcerers who, while not presenting detailed rules, does give a half-page sidebar of general guidelines because that's probably all we'll get on that topic.</li> <li><b>Chapter 2: Into the Maw</b> is all about the Lifeless ranging from the abominable Shuankhsen to other daemons of Duat like the slaughterers, jackal-men, and ghosts driven mad by centuries of sybaritic influence.</li> <li><b>Chapter 3: Memoirs of the Nile</b> finishes it off with the Deathless, both Arisen and Deceived. Millennia of magic chaining your soul to underworld spirits does wonders - and horrors - that aren't so easily defined by base mechanics. We know how this works - it's a <b>Night Horrors</b> book after all.</li> </ul>Then I'll die happy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}